WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.300
Letters on pencils.

2
00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:02.854
Pencils have letters.

3
00:00:03.014 --> 00:00:05.521
H means hard: pale, fine lines.

4
00:00:05.681 --> 00:00:07.957
B means black: soft, dark lines.

5
00:00:08.117 --> 00:00:10.207
The bigger the number, the stronger.

6
00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:12.874
A 6B pencil is darker than a 2B.

7
00:00:13.574 --> 00:00:14.317
Tone.

8
00:00:14.477 --> 00:00:16.753
Tone means how light or dark something is.

9
00:00:16.913 --> 00:00:22.114
With a few pencils and some charcoal, you can make every grey from almost white to almost black.

10
00:00:22.814 --> 00:00:24.022
Light and shade.

11
00:00:24.182 --> 00:00:28.547
When light shines on something, the side facing the light is bright.

12
00:00:28.707 --> 00:00:30.843
The brightest spot is the highlight.

13
00:00:31.003 --> 00:00:33.093
The side facing away is in shade.

14
00:00:33.253 --> 00:00:35.343
That is what makes a drawing look round.

15
00:00:36.043 --> 00:00:37.390
Cast shadows.

16
00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:41.033
A thing that blocks the light throws a shadow onto something else.

17
00:00:41.193 --> 00:00:42.725
That is a cast shadow.

18
00:00:42.885 --> 00:00:45.068
It always falls away from the light.
